---
title: 🌯 Halloumi Shawarma Wraps
author: Foodieholly
prep_time: 10 minutes
cook_time: 20 minutes
servings: 2
source: https://foodieholly.com/wprm_print/halloumi-shawarma-wraps
tags:
  - halloumi
  - wrap
  - middle eastern
  - quick
---

-- ============================================================
-- SALAD
-- ============================================================

Preheat your #oven{} to 180°C (350°F) and line an #oven tray{} with parchment paper.

Thinly slice the @red onion{1/2} and put it in a #mixing bowl{} with the @sumac{1%tsp} and the juice of the @lemon{1/2}. Let it sit for ~pickling{5%minutes} [- source: 5-10 minutes -] to soften and lightly pickle.

While it rests, dice the @cucumber{1/2} and @tomatoes{100%g}, and chop the @parsley{1%tbsp} and @dill{1%tbsp}. Add everything to the bowl, season with @black pepper{}, mix well and set aside.

-- ============================================================
-- HALLOUMI
-- ============================================================

Pat the @halloumi{220%g} dry with kitchen paper. Lay it flat on the board and, using a Y-shaped #potato peeler{}, peel it into long strips from top to bottom. If pieces break, start from another side or slice the rest as thinly as possible. -- Peeled strips have uneven edges that crisp better and catch more seasoning than slices. Optionally soak the halloumi in cold water for 10 minutes first to make it less salty.

In a second #mixing bowl{}, toss the strips gently with the @Greek yoghurt{1%tbsp}, @olive oil{1%tbsp} and @shawarma seasoning{1.5%tsp} [- source: 1-2 tsp; or mix ½ tsp each smoked paprika, cumin, ground coriander and garlic powder with ¼ tsp cinnamon and a pinch of black pepper -] until evenly coated.

Spread the halloumi out on the tray as much as possible and cover with foil or another tray. Bake covered for ~covered{10%minutes}, then uncover and bake for another ~uncovered{4%minutes} [- source: 3-5 minutes -] until lightly golden. Don't let it get too crispy, as it hardens as it cools. Rest for ~resting{2%minutes} so it firms up slightly.

-- ============================================================
-- ASSEMBLE
-- ============================================================

Warm the @flatbreads{2-3}. Spread the @garlic yoghurt{2%tbsp} (or garlic mayo, or Greek yoghurt mixed with garlic) over each base, add some chopped @lettuce{}, spoon over the tomato and cucumber salad, then top with a generous handful of the baked halloumi.

Finish with extra sauce and herbs if you like. Serve straight away while warm, or toast the wraps in a pan with a little oil.
